  "problem": "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $M?$\n\n- $(L\u2227M)\u2228M$\n- $M\u2227(L\u2227M)$\n- $M\u2228(L\u2227M)$",
  "worked_solution": "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nM\u2228(M\u2227L)\u2261M.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is logically equivalent to $M.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(L\u2227M)\u2228M & \u2261M\u2228(L\u2227M) \\\\  & \u2261M\u2228(M\u2227L) \\\\  & \u2261M.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is *not* logically equivalent to $M.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $M.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M\u2228(L\u2227M) & \u2261M\u2228(M\u2227L) \\\\  & \u2261M.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
